    "Scan of the 1948 edition of the Jupiter, Florida, topographic map at 1:24,000 scale (7.5 x 7.5 minute series), published by the U.S. Geological Survey and the Department of Commerce. Surveyed in 1947; aerial photographs from 1980; field checked in 1948; photo revised in 1983; last revised in 1983; printed in 1986.",
    "Variations: woodland tint. Sheet size: 24 x 28.3 inches. Printed projection: Polyconic; horizontal datum: NAD27. From the USGS Historical Topographic Map Collection."
